Description
Responsible for the implementation of the company's recruitment program, including job demand analysis, recruitment channel management, resume screening, and interview arrangements;
Manage recruitment channels, and establish and maintain the talent pool.
Develop and optimize the company's human resource management system and process, including recruitment, training, performance appraisal, salary management,t and other modules;
Organize and implement staff training programs to enhance the overall capability of the team;
Responsible for the handling of employee procedures such as entry, exit, and transfer and the management of employee files;
Pay attention to employee relations, solve internal conflicts of the team in time, and maintain a good corporate culture atmosphere;
Provide the company with advice related to labor law to ensure legal compliance;
Assisting the management in completing other HR-related matters.
Assist in the implementation of the performance appraisal system and follow up the application of appraisal results.
Responsible for the provision and analysis of salary accounting data to ensure the reasonable implementation of salary and benefit policies.
Requirements
College Degree or above, majoring in Human Resource Management, Business Management or other related majors is preferred;
2 years of relevant working experience (e.g. recruitment, training or employee relations);
Familiar with local labor laws and related laws and regulations, and have the ability to independently handle labor relations issues;
Excellent communication and coordination skills, strong stress resistance;
Proficient in the use of office software (Word, Excel, PPT, etc.);
Men are preferred, under 30 years old;

We are a conglomerate company based in Kaduna. We are seeking to employ experienced and skilled Accountants to join our team.
The ideal candidates should possess hands-on experience in accounting and have a strong understanding of financial principles. The position offers the opportunity to work in a dynamic environment
Key Responsibilities:
Prepare and maintain accurate financial records and reports.
Assist in the preparation of tax returns and financial statements.
Manage accounts payable/Creditors/suppliers, receivable/ Debtors and ensuring timely payment and receipts.
Analyze financial data and provide insights to improve financial performance;
Provide reports : monthly, quarterly, annually and management reports when required;
Ensure compliance with accounting policies, procedures, and regulations.
Any other job that may be assigned by management.
Requirements:
A Degree/ HND or Masters in Accounting, Finance, or a related field preferred;
Candidates with cognitive experience in a Rice mill, manufacturing, supplies and distribution companies would have an edge;
Proficient in Accounting software/ERP;
Professional certification like ICAN etc. is an additional advantage;
Strong knowledge of accounting principles, tax regulation, and financial reporting.
Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills.
Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities.
Ability to work independently and as part of a team.

